# Kill switch for the automated pipeline. Read by `bw pipeline` and `bw
# start` (src/cli.ts) and by ops/publish.sh — only the first line matters,
# and must be exactly `true` or `false`.
#
# While `true`:
#   - `bw pipeline` (cron) and `bw start` (`docker compose up`, container
#     entrypoint) print a message and exit immediately: no collect, extract,
#     detect, synthesize, export, or heartbeat, and no network or database
#     writes.
#   - ops/publish.sh refuses to commit/push and records itself as an ok
#     no-op, not a failure.
#   - Backups (ops/backup.sh, `bw ops backup`, the monthly verify-backup)
#     are NOT affected and keep running on the existing crontab — they still
#     write to the `runs` table, they just won't text you if one fails.
#   - No Telegram alerts of any kind go out while paused: the daily
#     pipeline/heartbeat alerts (suppressed because heartbeat never runs —
#     it lives inside the paused pipeline), and also backup/restic/
#     verify-backup failure alerts (explicitly suppressed in src/cli.ts's
#     `alertUnlessPaused`, since those run independently of the pipeline).
#     Manual commands (e.g. `bw ops heartbeat` run by hand) are unaffected
#     and still alert — this only silences the automated/cron paths.
#   - The container healthcheck will report unhealthy (no recent `collect`
#     run) — that's expected while paused, not a bug.
#
# Paused: 2026-09-08 — Nick asked to disable the project and its cron jobs
# without removing anything, so it can be flipped back on later. Extended
# 2026-09-09 to also silence backup/verify-backup Telegram alerts.
#
# To reactivate:
#   1. Change the first line above to `false` and commit.
#   2. On the homelab box: `git pull && docker compose up -d --build`
#      (rebuilds the image with the new flag; the crontab lines need no
#      changes — they were never touched).
